----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.  THE UPSILON LEVER, measured by re-running the pipeline at Upsilon x 1.5.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  gamma_v is a ratio of the MEASURED relative velocity to the NEWTONIAN prediction, and the Newtonian
  prediction uses component masses from a mass-luminosity relation.  Upsilon -> 1.5 Upsilon multiplies the
  predicted Newtonian velocity by sqrt(1.5), so gamma_v -> gamma_v/sqrt(1.5).  Re-run:
     [canonical] Upsilon x1.5 sends gamma_v to 0.9564 <= 1: THE ESTIMATOR HAS NO SOLUTION AT ALL.
     [alt      ] Upsilon x1.5 sends gamma_v to 0.9873 <= 1: THE ESTIMATOR HAS NO SOLUTION AT ALL.
  the analytic prediction is (d log M_b/d log gamma_v) x (-1/2):
     [canonical] analytic +4.09   measured +inf
     [alt      ] analytic +3.73   measured +inf
  [PASS] the Upsilon lever is LARGE and is reported against interest: a x1.5 error in the wide-binary mass-luminosity calibration destroys the estimator or moves the mass by more than a factor 2  [CAN FAIL]   (canonical inf, alt inf)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6.  THE RESTATEMENT TEST, executed rather than asserted.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ATTEMPT.  From v^4 = G M_b a_0 alone, a test particle's boost over Newton is g_obs/g_N = sqrt(a_0/g_int),
  a function of the system's OWN internal field.  Apply it to the wide-binary rung:
     [canonical]    5 kAU, 1.5 Msun: y = g_int/a_0 = 3.8023; BTFR boost in FORCE = 0.513 (gamma_v = 0.716); the law's B = 1.341 (gamma_v = 1.158)
     [canonical]   30 kAU, 1.5 Msun: y = g_int/a_0 = 0.1056; BTFR boost in FORCE = 3.077 (gamma_v = 1.754); the law's B = 1.341 (gamma_v = 1.158)
     [alt      ]    5 kAU, 1.5 Msun: y = g_int/a_0 = 3.1495; BTFR boost in FORCE = 0.563 (gamma_v = 0.751); the law's B = 1.341 (gamma_v = 1.158)
     [alt      ]   30 kAU, 1.5 Msun: y = g_int/a_0 = 0.0875; BTFR boost in FORCE = 3.381 (gamma_v = 1.839); the law's B = 1.341 (gamma_v = 1.158)
  The two disagree by a factor 2-4 and, decisively, the BTFR boost DEPENDS ON SEPARATION while B does not.
  So the mass estimator M_b = e(gamma_v^2) a_0 R_0^2/G cannot be produced by algebra on v^4 = G M_b a_0.
  VERDICT ON THE RESTATEMENT TEST: the derivation DOES NOT CLOSE -- this is not the BTFR in new clothes.
  BUT note what that buys: the content is the EXTERNAL-FIELD EFFECT, which is a standard and long-published
  part of MOND (Milgrom 1983, 1986; Bekenstein & Milgrom 1984; Famaey & McGaugh 2012 Living Review Sec 6.3).
  The g_int -> 0 coefficient nu(e)[1+L(e)/3] is the trace of the known anisotropic EFE dilation tensor, NOT
  a new object.  What would be new is only the INVERSION -- using it as a mass estimator.
  [PASS] the restatement test is executed and reported: the BTFR boost depends on separation, B does not, so the derivation does not close  [CAN FAIL]   (the two separations give different BTFR boosts, so no single number can come out of it)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.  THE ALTERNATIVE AND THE MUTATION CONTROLS.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  LambdaCDM/Newton: a 30 kAU wide binary sits inside the Galactic disc's smooth potential, and Newtonian
  gravity is LINEAR -- the Galaxy's field cancels from the relative motion exactly.  gamma_v = 1.000 with no
  free parameter.  Fed to this estimator, gamma_v = 1 gives e = infinity and M_b = infinity: the alternative's
  prediction is that the estimator has NO SOLUTION.  That is a sharp, falsifiable difference, and it is the
  whole content of the December test -- it is not new content added by the mass inversion.
     a_0 x 10        : M_b = 5.195e+11 Msun
     a_0 x 0.1       : M_b = 5.195e+09 Msun
     a_0 x 1 (truth) : M_b = 5.195e+10 Msun  (1.00x truth)
  [PASS] mutation control bites: a_0 x 10 changes the inferred baryonic mass by an order of magnitude  [CAN FAIL]   (5.195e+10 -> 5.195e+11 Msun)
  nu = 1 foil: with no kernel there is no boost, gamma_v = 1, and the estimator is undefined -- the same
  statement as the LambdaCDM alternative above.

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT ON CANDIDATE 3
======================================================================================================================
  [FAIL] (1) it is a relation between MEASURED quantities
         gamma_v will be measured, but M_b,MW comes out of it only after ASSUMING a point-mass Galaxy; the disc geometry factor is a 6-16% prior on the answer
  [PASS] (2) a_0 appears with a PREDICTED coefficient
         yes: a_0 enters as e a_0 R_0^2/G with nothing fitted
  [FAIL] (3) it holds across many systems to <= 0.1 dex
         it is a ONE-SYSTEM statement -- there is exactly one Milky Way, so 'scatter across systems' cannot even be defined; the propagated error from sigma_sys(gamma_v) = 0.02 alone is 0.071 dex-equivalent = 16% in mass
  [PASS] (4) nobody has stated it
         the inversion as a mass estimator is not in the literature; the EFE boost it inverts IS (Milgrom 1986; Famaey & McGaugh 2012 Sec 6.3), and must be credited
  [PASS] (5) it is NOT a restatement of v^4 = G M_b a_0
         confirmed by execution above: the BTFR boost depends on separation, B does not

  >>> 3 of 5 Kepler-grade criteria met.  CANDIDATE 3 IS NOT A SECOND LAW.
  >>> It is a COROLLARY of the December wide-binary test, and today it is exactly circular (check 2 fired):
      the frozen band was generated from an assumed M_b = 5.709e10 Msun and the inversion returns that mass.
  >>> Its one real use is as a CONSISTENCY TARGET for December: if gamma_v is measured and the inverted mass
      lands outside 6.0-7.3e10 Msun after the disc-geometry correction, the framework has a second problem
      beyond gamma_v itself.  On the frozen band that target is met on the ALT footing and missed LOW on the
      canonical one, which is a free footing discriminator -- worth 0.1 dex, not worth a law.

  UPSILON LEVER (the number the task asked for): d log M_b/d log Upsilon = UNDEFINED (no solution at Upsilon x1.5) / UNDEFINED   -- the LARGEST lever of the three candidates.

